{
  "dom_id": "step-q75001",
  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Find $|r(\\frac{\\pi }{3})|$ given that $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,6⟩.$",
  "worked_solution": "Evaluating the function at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),\\,6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2},\\,4\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2\\sqrt{3},\\,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(\\frac{\\pi }{3})| & =\\sqrt{{(1)}^{2}+{(2\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+(6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+12+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
